X-loop: s-news

Dear S-Plussers

I have encountered a (for me) strange behaviour of the neural network
provided
in the add-in library NNET in S-Plus2000. I have a dataset consisting of
667
samples with three predictor variables and one class variables with two
levels.

The neural network solutions to this classification problem are highly
unstable
producing frequent local minima with very poor predictions and ocassionally
very
good solutions.

When I change the scale of the predictor variables by dividing the numbers
with
100, the neral network solutions suddenly become very stable.

As I intend to apply cross-validation procedures to select good values for
the
parameters "size" and "decay" and also to compare with the performance of
alternative sets of predictors, this dependency on the scale of the
predictors
is critical.

Can anybody explain to me the reason for this?

regards

Rasmus
