Hi all,

Here is (hopefully) a simple lm() object question:

When we do a linear model, we get parameter and std. error estimates
among other things:

> summary(lm.out)

Call: lm(formula = yield ~ enddate, data = data2, na.action = na.exclude

)
Residuals:
     Min       1Q  Median      3Q   Max
 -0.5027 -0.05413 0.02241 0.07737 0.206

Coefficients:
               Value Std. Error  t value Pr(>|t|)
(Intercept)   4.3559   0.1219    35.7230   0.0000
    enddate  -0.0003   0.0000   -31.6737   0.0000

... and so forth ...

We can use  "lm.out$coefficients" to get the beta coefficients, but I
don't see the corresponding object available for the std. errors -- or
better yet, the variance-covariance matrix.

Anyone know how to get these standard errors and are willing to share
the knowledge?

Thanks in advance!

 -- Paul

